Active athletes: those who have participated in competitions (indicated by a non-zero number of starts in the year);
Mentors: refers to the coaches of the athletes;
Performances: measured by total points earned by the athlete;
Financial outcomes: total earnings of the athletes over the years.

NASDAQ refers to the National Association of Securities Dealers Automated Quotations, which is a global electronic marketplace for buying and selling securities; 
 A regular trading session refers to a standard trading day, usually between 9:30 am and 4:00 pm ET, excluding extended hours or holiday sessions;
 A prolific trader is someone who actively engages in buying and selling securities, with 'most prolific' referring to those with the highest trading activity.

- 'sailed through the stormy seas of competition' refers to boats that have completed races;
- 'completed their voyages' refers to races with a status of 'completed';
- 'lasted longer than a single hour' refers to races with a duration greater than 1 hour, ranging up to 6 hours or more.

- 'Total sales value' is the sum of all sale prices in a neighbourhood;
- 'Average price per square foot' is calculated by dividing the sale price by the average square footage;
- 'Preferred neighbourhoods' are the areas where buyers have expressed a preference to live.

- "Top 3 in performance" refers to the top 3 car models based on their performance value within each model year and origin;
- "Frequently visited more than 5 times" means the car models have been accessed more than 5 times in the access logs;
- "Last seen in the year 2023" indicates the most recent access to the car models was in the year 2023.
